assets/*.mov
assets/*.mp4
assets/*.webm

# Swappable centre-video runtime state, NEVER commit. Attacker-influenceable
# uploaded media + per-NUC takeover manifest. Keeping these out of the public
# repo is the page-side edge of M-GV12 (grace-house-video-upload threat model).
assets/uploads/
assets/now-playing.json

# Phase A bench harness, local test only, never ships.
option-b/bench.html

# Gate A/B test harness output (screenshots) + local deps
test/shots/
test/node_modules/

# Phase B ingest runtime state (when the guard runs with repo-relative defaults)
# + the hostile fixture set. Bench-only, never ship.
ingest/.work/
ingest/.state/
test/fixtures/

# Phase C/D watcher runtime state (repo-relative defaults, bench only).
ingest/.incoming/
ingest/.watchstate/
ingest/mockdrive/

# ---- PORTAL (Round 2) runtime state + secrets — NEVER COMMIT (M-GV15) ----
# portal.env holds PORTAL_SECRET (signs sessions) + PORTAL_PASSWORD_HASH. On the
# NUC it lives at /opt/grace-portal (outside the repo); these ignore the paths a
# repo-relative dev run would create. The public repo must never carry them.
portal/portal.env
portal/.state/
portal/.intake/
portal/static/uploads/

# ---- CREDENTIALS / ENDPOINT IDENTIFIERS — NEVER COMMIT (M-GV8) ----
# The repo is PUBLIC. rclone.conf holds the Drive OAuth refresh token; watch.env
# holds ntfy topics; the credential-setup doc holds the Drive folder ID (an
# upload-endpoint identifier the threat model requires kept out of the repo).
**/rclone.conf
ingest/.config/
ingest/watch.env
ingest/PHASE-C-credential-setup.md

# Licensed font binaries. fsType permits EMBEDDING, not redistribution, and
# this repository is public. Deploy them to the NUC by scp instead.
**/fonts/*.ttf
**/fonts/*.otf
**/fonts/*.woff
**/fonts/*.woff2
